Z||000001||lowCG||10-15-1999||02:04 AM||||Windage trays go right under your crankshaft,and reduce the amount of oil from in the pan that is whipped up by the fast moving parts(crankshaft,and rods).Usually bolts onto a couple of main bearing cap bolts.Can give you a few(10-20)good free horsepower at higher revs,where you want it.<BR>Where did you see this part for the Fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lynx||10-15-1999||02:40 AM||||Not to answer for him but you can get this windage tray from the Fiero store part#52870 and they cost $59.95. Damn i didnt know they actually made horsepower. I was just going to put one in my 85GT because is helps get oil to the engine at all times. And the engine i have blew because of a rod knock.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||10-15-1999||11:53 AM||||I doubt you will see a 10-20 hp gain by purchasing the windage tray from the fiero store or any windage tray.  Maybe 1-2 at the most.  The job of the windage tray is to prevent the crank from throwing oil away from the oil pump pickup which would starve the engien of oil.<P>What you want that will add hp will be a crank scraper.  What this does is prevent little oil droplets from collecting on the cranksahft and rod ends making the engien unbalanced and adding to the reciprocating assembly of the engine.  These have been dyno proven in big blocks to give up to 20 hp.  Now you won't see a 20 hp increase on the Fiero but a 5 hp gain from this mod is reasonable.   Its too bad no one manufacturs a crank scraper for the 2.8/3.1's out there so if you want one you are going to have to make it yourself.<P>I have a question though.  Can this samme windage tray from the Fiero Store work with a 3.1 crank?  Will the longer throws of the 3.1 allow the crank or rods hit the tray?  Anyone with first hand experience with this?||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||10-15-1999||11:55 AM||||Looking at the 20hp,I'd posted as a possible gain;once again that's probably on a larger engine,however.But I'd say 10,no problem.||||reg||11
Z||000005||theogre||10-15-1999||01:21 PM||||a Vindage tray? must be some new way to make wine.<P>A wind tray just helps keep the oil from getting wiped into foam by the crank.<P>Depending on the tray it can also block oil movement away from the pickup caused by lateral and/or line G forces durring corning or hard braking/launching.<P>It's main job is to prevent oil starvation.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fastonpumpgas||10-16-1999||07:32 AM||||in my opinion, i think it is only worth it if you are going to run high RMP's for a long period of time, you might get alittle hp out of it, remember a stock 2.8 was rated only at 133hp, where as a BB can be 400+ . I would do it more for a safe guard, alot of 2.8 throw the 1st and 4th rod bearing, i think it has something to do with the  harmonic balancer, but that is my guest.  But does anyone know if the windage tray with clear the 3.1 crank ?||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroshop||10-16-1999||10:46 AM||||I've installed several vindage trays and they do not increase HP. All they do is help lubricate the engine and also prevent oil from moving away from the oil pickup during high speed and high rpm||||reg||1
